    "content": "{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cstdlib>\\n\\nstatic const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\\nstatic char buf[BUFSIZE];\\nstatic int pos = 0, len = 0;\\n\\ninline char getChar() {\\n    if (pos >= len) {\\n        len = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\\n        pos = 0;\\n    }\\n    return buf[pos++];\\n}\\n\\ninline int readInt() {\\n    char c;\\n    do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ');\\n    int sign = 1;\\n    if (c == '-') { sign = -1; c = getChar(); }\\n    int x = c - '0';\\n    for (;;) {\\n        c = getChar();\\n        if (c < '0' || c > '9') break;\\n        x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\\n    }\\n    return sign * x;\\n}\\n\\nstatic inline int maxWindow(const int* col, int n, int s) {\\n    int cur = 0;\\n    for (int i = 0; i < s; ++i) cur += col[i];\\n    int mx = cur;\\n    const int* add = col + s;\\n    const int* sub = col;\\n    for (int j = s; j < n; ++j, ++add, ++sub) {\\n        cur += *add - *sub;\\n        if (cur > mx) mx = cur;\\n    }\\n    return mx;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n = readInt();\\n    int s = readInt();\\n\\n    int* colSum = static_cast<int*>(calloc(n, sizeof(int)));\\n    int* rows = static_cast<int*>(malloc(sizeof(int) * (size_t)s * n));\\n    if (!colSum || !rows) return 1;\\n\\n    for (int r = 0; r < s; ++r) {\\n        int* row = rows + (size_t)r * n;\\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\\n            int v = readInt();\\n            row[c] = v;\\n            colSum[c] += v;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    int mx = maxWindow(colSum, n, s);\\n\\n    for (int r = s; r < n; ++r) {\\n        int ringPos = r % s;\\n        int* row = rows + (size_t)ringPos * n;\\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\\n            int old = row[c];\\n            int v = readInt();\\n            row[c] = v;\\n            colSum[c] += v - old;\\n        }\\n        int curMax = maxWindow(colSum, n, s);\\n        if (curMax > mx) mx = curMax;\\n    }\\n\\n    printf(\\\"%d\\\\n\\\", mx);\\n\\n    free(rows);\\n    free(colSum);\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/solution.cpp\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"Streaming the matrix row-by-row into a flat ring buffer of only S rows, maintaining vertical column sums for the current S-row window, and scanning horizontal windows over that contiguous colSum array replaces the snake traversal's O(S*N^2) strided memory accesses with O(N^2) sequential streaming accesses. This improves cache locality and reduces memory traffic while keeping intermediate sliding-window values within 32-bit range on valid inputs.\",\"notes\":\"Uses a custom fread-based integer parser to avoid iostream overhead, allocates only S*N ints instead of the full NxN matrix, and updates column sums in one fused pass per input row by subtracting the overwritten ring-buffer value before storing the new value. The horizontal maximum is computed with a simple sliding window over colSum; no prefix-sum array is used so intermediate values remain actual SxS submatrix sums rather than potentially larger cumulative totals.\",\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Replace full NxN vector-of-vectors storage with a flat ring buffer of exactly S rows, reducing memory footprint and improving sequential locality.\",\"Fuse input parsing with column-sum maintenance: each new row is read once, the oldest row in the ring is subtracted from colSum, and the new row is added to colSum in the same inner loop.\",\"Replace snake-order O(S*N^2) window updates with a per-bottom-row horizontal sliding-window scan over contiguous colSum entries, giving O(N^2) total work after streaming input.\"]}",
